# What Git never tracks in this repository. Files of your own OS or editor
# that are not listed here belong in your global ignore file
# (git config --global core.excludesFile).

# Build and test output ------------------------------------------------------
# `task clean` removes these.
/bin/
/dist/
# `task cover`.
/coverage.out
/coverage.html
# Test binaries from `go test -c`.
*.test
*.tmp
# Note: testdata/fuzz/ is NOT ignored: the inputs `go test -fuzz` saves there
# are regression tests and must be committed.

# Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------------
# A safety net for AGENTS.md "Security": credentials never enter the
# repository. Tests create their certificates at run time; a fixture that
# really needs one of these names is added with `git add -f`.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Editors and OS -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
# VS Code: only the shared settings are tracked (docs/development.md,
# "Editors and dev container"); launch configs, workspaces and other personal
# files stay local. .zed/ and .devcontainer/ are tracked as a whole.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# AI agents ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code: .claude/settings.json is shared (it denies reading credentials
# and force pushes); settings.local.json holds personal permissions.
.claude/settings.local.json
# Working material of agents: briefs, plans, review reports. They may quote
# code and are not reviewed for publication (docs/development-workflow.md).
.plans/
